# TypeScript Style

- Use `const` by default; `let` only when reassignment is needed
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use `satisfies` for type-safe object literals when appropriate
- Explicit return types on exported functions
- Destructure parameters when 3+ fields
- Errors: always wrap in typed custom errors, never swallow silently
